# Pipistrel SW121 / SW128 — Flight Test Campaign

A structured manned-aircraft flight-test campaign at **Politecnico di Milano** comparing conventional and electric aircraft through performance and stability testing.

The programme comprised **four flights and approximately 100 directed test points**.

## My Role

**Team Leader / On-board Flight Test Engineer — 2-member team**

I was responsible for:

- defining objectives, test points and test sequencing;
- flight-test planning, flight cards and instrumentation requirements;
- Test Hazard Analysis and coordination with the Flight Test Pilot;
- in-flight test execution and data recording;
- post-flight data reduction using MATLAB and Dewesoft;
- comparison with POH and certification-oriented reference values;
- evaluation of anomalies, test validity and recommendations for re-testing.

The work covered take-off and landing performance, stall behaviour and longitudinal dynamic stability, with a strong focus on **repeatability, safety and engineering judgement**.
